.TH ZERODDS-MQTT-BRIDGED.YAML 5 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-mqtt-bridged.yaml \- configuration file for zerodds-mqtt-bridged(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/zerodds/mqtt-bridged.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
YAML document describing how the MQTT bridge daemon maps DDS topics onto MQTT
topics. The schema is the one of
.IR zerodds-mqtt-bridge-1.0 " \(sc3;"
the parser that reads it is
.IR crates/mqtt-bridge/src/daemon/config.rs::load_from_str .
.PP
Top-level keys:
.BR domain ", " log_level ", " mqtt ", " auth ", " acl ", " metrics ", " topics .
.PP
An unknown top-level key is
.I not
a parse error. The daemon logs a WARN line on stderr and starts with the
defaults \(em watch the WARN log.
.PP
.BI ${VAR} " and " ${VAR:-default}
are substituted from the environment before the document is parsed, so
credentials belong in the environment, not in the file.
.SH KEYS
.SS Top level
.TP
.B domain
Integer DDS domain ID. Default
.IR 0 .
.TP
.B log_level
.IR trace " | " debug " | " info " | " warn " | " error .
.SS mqtt
.TP
.B broker_url
.IR mqtt:// ", " mqtts:// ", " ws:// " or " wss://
URL of the broker, e.g.
.IR "mqtt://localhost:1883"
or
.IR "wss://broker:443/mqtt" .
The WebSocket schemes carry MQTT in binary frames (MQTT 5.0 \(sc6); the path
defaults to
.IR /mqtt .
.TP
.B client_id
MQTT client identifier; must be unique on the broker.
.TP
.B drain_timeout_secs
Seconds the shutdown waits for the broker's acknowledgements of QoS 1/2
messages before DISCONNECT (spec \(sc9.2). Default 30.
.TP
.B keep_alive_secs
CONNECT keep-alive in seconds.
.TP
.B clean_start
Boolean.
.I false
keeps the session across a reconnect.
.TP
.B username ", " password
Legacy credentials for the CONNECT packet. They are a fallback:
.BR auth.username " and " auth.password
win when both are set.
.TP
.B tls
Sub-map with
.B enabled
(boolean),
.B ca_file
(trust anchor for the broker certificate),
.BR cert_file " and " key_file
(client material for mTLS) and
.B server_name
(SNI/hostname override). The client keys are named
.BR cert_file / key_file ,
not
.IR client_cert_file / client_key_file .
.SS auth
.TP
.B mode
.IR none " | " bearer " | " sasl " | " sasl_plain " | " mtls " (\(sc7.2)."
.TP
.B bearer_token
Token sent as the CONNECT password when
.B mode
is
.IR bearer .
.TP
.B bearer_subject
Subject that single token authenticates as.
.TP
.B username ", " password
SASL-PLAIN credentials towards the broker.
.TP
.B sasl_users
Map
.IR user: password
used by the daemon-internal ACL path to validate inbound subjects.
.SS acl
Daemon-side access control, evaluated before MQTT. The subject is taken from
the TLS certificate DN, the MQTT username or the JWT
.I sub
claim, in that order.
.TP
.B default_deny
Boolean.
.I true
denies a topic no rule names, also without any rule;
.I false
opens the unnamed rest. Not set: a topic no rule names is denied once a
rule exists or an auth mode other than
.I none
is set; with neither, every topic is open.
.TP
.B rules
List of subject-keyed rules. Each entry carries
.B subject
plus the topic pattern lists
.BR allow_publish " and " allow_subscribe .
The daemon inverts this into a topic-keyed map.
.SS metrics
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. Turns on the admin endpoint serving
.IR /metrics ", " /catalog " and " /healthz .
.TP
.B listen
Admin listen address. Default
.IR "127.0.0.1:9092"
when
.B enabled
is true; each bridge daemon has its own port, so several run on one
host without a collision.
The key is
.BR listen ,
not
.IR address .
.SS topics (list)
.TP
.B dds_name
DDS topic name.
.TP
.B dds_type
Fully-qualified IDL type.
.TP
.B mqtt_topic
MQTT topic or filter. Defaults to a slug of
.BR dds_name .
.TP
.B direction
.IR in " | " out " | " bidir .
.I in
carries MQTT messages from the broker into DDS (the daemon subscribes on
the broker and creates a DataWriter),
.I out
carries DDS samples to the broker (a DataReader, published to
.BR mqtt_topic ),
.I bidir
both. Default
.IR bidir .
.TP
.B mqtt_qos
.IR 0 " | " 1 " | " 2 .
.TP
.B retain
Boolean; sets the MQTT retain flag on published messages.
.TP
.B qos
DDS QoS sub-map with
.BR reliability ", " durability " and "
.B history
carrying
.BR depth .
.SH EXAMPLES
See
.IR /usr/share/zerodds/configs/mqtt-bridged.yaml.example .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-mqtt-bridged (1),
.BR zerodds-xmlc (1).
